# The Quota: its own ruleset. Gameplay engineer, 2026-10-21. Private.
# The slice used to borrow Low Water's whole ruleset (../act1/rules.lwd), and with it the Gullet's
# character creation. This file keeps what the Quota's scenes use: the four compartments and the
# sixteen voices (since 2026-10-23 the four great traits and the sixteen traits), with the same ids, so the voice sheets and the checks read as before. It leaves
# out the Kit, the meters, the Precedents and the Gullet's items.
# There is no creation screen. The class choice at q.start is the start: the shell makes the plain
# sheet (start-archetype), and the choice calls become(q.ned) or become(q.will), which puts the
# chosen man's sheet in its place. The figure follows from @meta player-figure.

@rules
check-mode: fixed
xp-per-level: 1
points-per-level: 1
skill-cap: 4
creation-points: 11
creation: none
start-archetype: q.plain
attr-min: 1
attr-max: 5
cabinet-slots: 3
cabinet-slots-max: 6
forget-cost: 1
rep-min: -3
rep-max: 3
autosave-minutes: 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the four great traits (the compartments)
# The traits pass, 2026-10-23 (design/TRAITS.md, design/TRAITS-RENAME.md): every compartment and voice is a quality or
# a vice the character carries, and each one is a being he meets and fights in the inner arena. The ids are the old
# ones (pen, coat, hat, nose; sum, precedent and the rest), kept because the scenes, the checks, the saves and the
# combat build read them; the names and what each one is are new. combat/data/traits.mjs holds the same table and
# a test keeps the two in step.
@attr pen
name: SUSPICION
short: READ
about: What you see coming: the lie, the light sack, the shoulder before the blow. Reading blows early, weak points, breath.

@attr coat
name: HARDNESS
short: ENDURE
about: What you can take: cold, a blow, a load, a night on your feet. Standing, the weight you carry, the heavy tools.

@attr hat
name: AUTHORITY
short: END
about: How you make a thing stop: the look that ends a quarrel, the word that ends a fight. People give in sooner.

@attr nose
name: FEAR
short: EVADE
about: How you get out of the way: a step aside, a shadow, the door nobody saw you use. Dodges, footing, getting clear.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the sixteen traits (the voices)
@skill sum
name: PRUDENCE
attr: pen
about: Knows what a thing weighs and what it's worth, and keeps quiet about it. In a fight: swings cost less breath; the stick, the fid and the spanner hit harder.

@skill precedent
name: LOYALTY
attr: pen
about: Your family's words in your mouth. What your father did, you do. In a fight: finds the weak point after a blow you read.

@skill smallprint
name: COWARDICE
attr: pen
about: Finds the reason it was never your job. Quick to see a way out. In a fight: no tool of its own. It talks, and you meet its body inside.

@skill carbon
name: GUILT
attr: pen
about: Puts the scene back as it happened, and makes you stand in it. In a fight: reads a blow earlier and finds the weak point; the marlinspike and the fid.

@skill knees
name: WEARINESS
attr: coat
about: Stairs, cold, the long day. Wants to sit down. Gets you through by wanting less. In a fight: more breath; the roll carries further; the oar, the beetle and bare hands.

@skill ballast
name: OBEDIENCE
attr: coat
about: Holds the line it's given. Keeps you on your feet when the ground moves. In a fight: poise; the pole, the chain and the hammer.

@skill pride
name: VANITY
attr: coat
about: Needs to be seen and liked. Keeps your back straight in a good coat. In a fight: the case catches a longer window; the key and the bell jar.

@skill grip
name: APPETITE
attr: coat
about: The hands' wanting: the bread, the door, the man. Remembers in the knuckles. In a fight: blows break poise; the hammer, the crowbar and bare hands.

@skill condolence
name: TENDERNESS
attr: hat
about: Sees the hurt in people and wants to hold on. Holds on too long. In a fight: people give in sooner; the bell jar.

@skill formletter
name: CONTEMPT
attr: hat
about: Talks down. Makes a man feel the size he is. In a fight: people give in sooner; the case and the pole.

@skill chit
name: JEALOUSY
attr: hat
about: Sees what the other man has and what he paid. Never lets it go. In a fight: no tool of its own. It talks, and you meet its body inside.

@skill hearsay
name: SPITE
attr: hat
about: Says the thing that will hurt, and says it where it will spread. In a fight: people give in sooner.

@skill smell
name: DISGUST
attr: nose
about: Smells sickness, smoke, the store that isn't empty. Wants to wash its hands of people. In a fight: the eel spear.

@skill dark
name: DREAD
attr: nose
about: Knows what's coming before it comes. Sees in the dark. In a fight: longer dodges; the knife and the stick.

@skill undertow
name: SHAME
attr: nose
about: Knows what people hide because it hides things too. Pulls you toward it. In a fight: reads a blow earlier; the crowbar.

@skill salt
name: NERVE
attr: nose
about: The body's nerve: weather in the joints, the will to go first. In a fight: longer dodges; the eel spear, the tiller, the boathook and the oar.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- who people answer to
@faction district
name: The district
about: The office, the militia post, and the families of the men who work there.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you have turned on your own
tier: 0 thinks you are one of them
tier: 2 thinks you can be relied on

@faction directorate
name: The Directorate
about: Commissioner Pask and the requisition squads. Arlen's figures, in Arlen's hand.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are a saboteur
tier: 0 thinks you are a district official
tier: 2 thinks you are reliable

@faction chairmen
name: The brigade chairmen
about: Krall and men like him, who send their carts heaped and want the district.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are in the way
tier: 0 thinks you can be worked with
tier: 2 thinks you are useful

@faction millstreet
name: Mill Street
about: The households of the mill and the yards below the square.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are the office's man
tier: 0 is waiting to see
tier: 2 thinks you are on their side

@faction hesh
name: The Hesh families
about: The herders from the hills and the hands who came down to work the harvests.
start: 0
tier: -3 thinks you are the census with a gun
tier: 0 does not trust you
tier: 2 trusts you, a little

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what they wear (combat/data/build.mjs CLOTHING: as the Shelf coat)
@item c.q_overcoat
name: The inspector's overcoat
slot: coat
warm: 2
mod: skill.pride +1
about: District issue, turned once at the cuffs.

@item c.q_hat
name: The good hat
slot: hat
mod: skill.formletter +1
about: Black felt. People who have stood in the queue by the scale know it.

@item c.q_greatcoat
name: The militia greatcoat
slot: coat
warm: 2
mod: skill.pride +1
about: Grey, with the district's number on the collar.

@item c.q_cap
name: The militia cap
slot: hat
about: A peaked cap with the badge sewn on.

@item w.stick
name: Ned's blackthorn stick
slot: hand
about: For the walk out to the villages. He tries the ruts with it before he puts his weight on them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the sheets
# The plain sheet stands until the choice at q.start; it is never played.
@archetype q.plain
name: The Upper Town
about: Before the choice at the tower.
attr: pen 3
attr: coat 3
attr: hat 3
attr: nose 2

@archetype q.ned
name: Ned Furrowe
about: District inspector. He stands at the scale when the villages' grain is weighed.
attr: pen 4
attr: coat 2
attr: hat 3
attr: nose 2
skill: sum 4
skill: precedent 2
skill: smallprint 2
skill: carbon 2
skill: condolence 1
skill: chit 1
skill: formletter 1
skill: pride 1
item: c.q_overcoat 1
item: c.q_hat 1
item: w.stick 1

@archetype q.will
name: Will Brack
about: Sergeant of militia. He keeps the cells and the road post.
attr: pen 2
attr: coat 4
attr: hat 2
attr: nose 3
skill: knees 2
skill: ballast 2
skill: pride 2
skill: grip 2
skill: salt 1
skill: smell 1
item: c.q_greatcoat 1
item: c.q_cap 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- day forty-one on the plain
# The plain has no tide. Frost all day; the wind gets up after noon and brings snow at dusk.
@day q_day41
tide: none
at: 05:50 daylight 0
at: 07:20 daylight 0
at: 08:10 daylight 0.7
at: 15:10 daylight 0.7
at: 16:10 daylight 0
at: 05:50 temp -9
at: 13:00 temp -4
at: 18:00 temp -8
at: 23:59 temp -12
at: 05:50 frost 1
at: 05:50 wind.speed 3
at: 12:30 wind.speed 4
at: 14:00 wind.speed 9
at: 20:00 wind.speed 11
at: 05:50 wind.dir 20
at: 05:50 snow 0
at: 16:30 snow 0
at: 17:30 snow 1
at: 21:00 snow 2.5

# The menu and the day's clock (UI and UX lead, 2026-10-23; DECISIONS-2026-10-22, "Retire the tide and the
# Daybook"). menu: the pause menu's pages in order, plainly named (ui/daybook.mjs): Character, Inventory, Map,
# Journal. No Record page: the read-back is never shown (q_readback.lwd), the witness scene carries it. hud-week:
# day 41, the act's first day, was a Wednesday (q_cells.lwd), so a later day's clock carries its weekday.
@meta
menu: build pack map
hud-week: Wednesday
